WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.740
Complete the order-support assistant in stages: deterministic loop, live local-model adapter, evaluated

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:11.796
retrieval, bounded memory, approval proposal storage, and operational measurements.

00:00:11.946 --> 00:00:14.487
Keep the business goal narrow enough to validate.

00:00:14.637 --> 00:00:21.092
Your portfolio should include a problem statement, architecture diagram, runnable instructions, tests,

00:00:21.092 --> 00:00:24.858
evaluation results, and a discussion of limitations.

00:00:25.008 --> 00:00:29.073
For interviews, explain requirements before naming libraries.

00:00:29.223 --> 00:00:31.987
Trace one successful request and one failure.

00:00:32.137 --> 00:00:37.352
State which component enforces identity, where an effect becomes durable, how retries

00:00:37.352 --> 00:00:40.394
behave, and what evidence supports answer quality.

00:00:40.544 --> 00:00:43.987
Distinguish an implemented capability from a design proposal.

00:00:44.137 --> 00:00:47.837
Clear boundaries and measured tradeoffs are stronger than a long list of

00:00:47.837 --> 00:00:48.454
AI terms.

00:00:48.604 --> 00:00:53.663
Additional projects include a read-only incident assistant using synthetic logs, a catalog-description

00:00:53.663 --> 00:00:58.722
reviewer that proposes edits for approval, and a document extractor that validates

00:00:58.722 --> 00:01:00.408
fields against a schema.

00:01:00.558 --> 00:01:03.029
Each should begin with a non-agent baseline.

00:01:03.179 --> 00:01:06.998
Do not connect the learning projects to office systems or real customer

00:01:06.998 --> 00:01:07.316
data.

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:12.725
Give a 15-minute design explanation: five minutes for requirements and architecture, five

00:01:12.725 --> 00:01:16.669
for failure handling, and five for evaluation and tradeoffs.

00:01:16.819 --> 00:01:20.879
Have another person introduce a malicious document and a provider timeout.

00:01:21.029 --> 00:01:27.331
A strong response preserves tenant isolation, rejects invented actions, bounds work, reports

00:01:27.331 --> 00:01:29.432
uncertainty, and explains recovery.

00:01:29.582 --> 00:01:35.414
Score yourself out of five on correctness, evidence, failure handling, clarity, and

00:01:35.414 --> 00:01:35.900
tradeoffs.

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:39.239
Redo the weakest section with a concrete test or measurement.

00:01:39.389 --> 00:01:40.060
Question.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:43.226
How would you design an agent for every business use case?

00:01:43.376 --> 00:01:43.952
Answer.

00:01:44.102 --> 00:01:47.356
Start by rejecting the premise of one universal design.

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:54.148
Classify read-only versus state-changing tasks, risk, data access, latency, and correctness needs,

00:01:54.148 --> 00:01:56.362
then choose suitable workflows.

00:01:56.512 --> 00:01:57.184
Question.

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:59.577
What should you show in a portfolio demo?

00:01:59.727 --> 00:02:00.304
Answer.

00:02:00.454 --> 00:02:05.778
A working happy path and a meaningful failure path, with commands, tests,

00:02:05.778 --> 00:02:07.997
evaluation evidence, and honest limits.
